03d8f3d6887" :question/math-academy-id "q-82372" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the exact solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-{90}^{∘})=-1$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-{90}^{∘} & =-{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={90}^{∘}-{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={45}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={225}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ So, the solutions are $x={45}^{∘},{225}^{∘}.$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is $45\\cdot 225=10\\,125.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-82372/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f40f50e-49a7-5eda-b642-dc7085569b23"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82372"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274622/field-1/a5bcf5044d7131cdf0d721e80125a87ad3d00df1e947910bf38c9dd3889981de" :answer/id #uuid "7b04c5fc-1efe-5d6b-9ff8-953fa6c02318" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "81" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274622/field-1/71ec7720d7077a8c88c1c4a9c53a3f81078793450c23aec02efcc43f1fc689b6" :answer/id #uuid "2d4d69ff-cbd4-5ad3-9984-f9be4f9f1151" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "82" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274622/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ec41c19-5cd5-53c3-b05a-fb7029122057" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.t