_{3}=$\n{{field-3}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{5x}{3})+4 & =0 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{5x}{3}) & =-4 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{5x}{3}) & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x}{3} & =-{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-{27}^{∘}+n\\cdot {108}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={81}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={189}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x={297}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ \n\nSo, the solutions to the equation, in ascending order, are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={81}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={189}^{∘},\\,{x}_{3}={297}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-274622/field-1" "q-274622/field-2" "q-274622/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f40f50e-49a7-5eda-b642-dc7085569b23"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274622"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121557/selection/fa2764e4d443b0fd1a8b9b79f38b985d2b576f72681c3b867c06cfeb24c839e4" :answer/id #uuid "6280b1cf-f281-51b8-a12c-b2e37a73d5ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "360" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121557/selection/6d5e653a0cc5c6e6fc44c5c3386727c89009586dc5171332dccb4c794ca30987" :answer/id #uuid "fa4f6f1f-e6b0-5df4-93d6-4ed188f077a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "330" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121557/selection/129e7786d72c790258971b5cb63148b0266c5cb2f913b1160289769eba3b4e49" :answer/id #uu