et\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & =-{180}^{∘}+n\\cdot {720}^{∘} \\\\ x & =-{36}^{∘}+n\\cdot {144}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={108}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={252}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ So, the solutions are $x={108}^{∘},{252}^{∘}.$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$ is $108+252=360.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121557/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f40f50e-49a7-5eda-b642-dc7085569b23"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121557"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328331/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "a43a6a5a-e0ea-56ff-945b-44d2f8e03a4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328331/field-1/e645b0f714e0f14adf4a4392c1fd41e203b4d4c946a42f546b48043b8700d60e" :answer/id #uuid "4486a80f-6b4c-5bc0-970e-2f81b292afd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "31" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328331/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "81d2051c-31b1-5c0c-a8bc-97a8a739d081" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328331/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-328331/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" "q-328331/field-1/e645b0f714e0f14adf4a4392c1fd41e203b4d4c946a42f546b48043b8700d60e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328331/field-2/407a8c9dd7706a5c0017938bdc16d552cb404ed5280e2197eaee2471cbb5128e" :answer/id #uuid "b0dc3ab0-ab2e-5484-95e5-b7a2f76a4431" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "210" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328331/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd7be71-cfb7-5237-b832-e4deffc9ea11" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328331/field-2/407a8c9dd7706a5c0017938bdc16d552cb404ed5280e2197eaee2471cbb5128e" :answer-field/choices ["q-328331/field-2/407a8c9dd7706a5c0017938bdc16d552cb404ed5280e2197eaee2471cbb5128e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328331" :question/id #uuid "12201c76-6367-5057-b138-d852f6b5dca8" :question/math-academy-id "q-328331" :question/problem "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the **exact solutions** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+{30}^{∘})=\\sqrt{3},$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+{30}^{∘} & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={60}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={30}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={210}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ \n\nSo, in ascending order,  the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={30}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={210}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-328331/field-1" "q-328331/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f40f50e-49a7-5eda-b642-dc7085569b23"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328331"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274700/field-1/608b697f811192589eec3729e28e5d056be7cd5127af1a846d717a33508ae203" :answer/id #uuid "af98